# HPC-first job execution

For this project (`/common/omarmlab/members/anh/panda_project`):

- **Never** run long or heavy jobs on the login node (`esplhpccompbio-lv01`).
- **Always** submit via `sbatch scripts/slurm_*.sh` on partition `defq`.
- Use existing Slurm templates in `scripts/`:
  - `slurm_clean_dataset.sh` — full mask QC
  - `slurm_scan_pen_marks.sh` — pen mark scan (`--resume` if checkpoint exists)
  - `slurm_verify_mask_balance.sh` — L0 vs pyramid balance check
  - `slurm_qc_bug_audit.sh` — grade-mismatch bug audit
  - `slurm_compare_trident_patches.sh` — Trident-Otsu vs naive-grid patch comparison
- Slurm headers: `#SBATCH --partition=defq`, `-o %j.out`, `-e %j.err`
- Env: `module load miniconda3/23.11.0-2`, `conda activate wsi_seg`, `source .env.hpc`
- For chunked L0 mask reads / full-slide scans: request **32G** mem; pen mark thumbnails: **16G** is enough.
- If a login-node job is already running, stop it and resubmit on Slurm with `--resume` when checkpoints exist.
